  "term": "hysterical blindness",
  "definition": "Hysterical blindness is an apparent loss of sight in hysteria that is described here as not being a true absence of visual perception. The passage says the person may seem blind to ordinary awareness, while visual impressions are still taken in by a split-off or submerged consciousness and can show themselves indirectly, such as through automatic responses.",
